\chapter*{Acknowledgements}

I would like to thank my committee members --- Robert Goldstone, Yong-Yeol Ahn, Peter Todd, Eliot Smith, and Nathaniel Geiger --- for their time, feedback, and contributions to this work. I am particularly grateful to Yong-Yeol Ahn and Robert Goldstone for their continued support throughout my extended doctoral studies. Their willingness to advocate for me, including helping secure teaching opportunities during periods of uncertainty, provided both the financial stability and time necessary for me to continue my development as a researcher and reach the completion of this degree. 
Additionally, I am grateful to the National Science Foundation for supporting research included in this dissertation. I am especially grateful to Nathaniel Geiger for making it possible for me to participate in that work and for his guidance throughout the development of this dissertation.

My thanks also go to the many colleagues qua friends and collaborators who shared pieces of their experience with me in conversations over coffee and coworking sessions over the years. In particular, I am grateful to Sebahat G\"ok, Marina Dubova, Priyamvada Modak, Varun Rao, and Eleanor Schille-Hudson. 
Your words of insight into your process and your support became the bricks that helped me put together an understanding of the craft and life of research. 

I would also like to thank the administrative staff who helped me navigate the many logistical challenges of graduate school, especially Tara Holbrook, Beverly Diekhoff, and Joshua Kemp. Their timely responses and willingness to help made managing administrative paperwork and deadlines significantly easier. 

I am grateful to the friends and community members who supported me outside of academia. I would like to thank Nate, Tyler, and Joc for your willingness to listen and corroborate moments of struggle, and for standing with me in times when I was not sure how to stand myself. To members of my queer and artistic communities --- especially Ken, Aether, Keith, and Scott --- thank you for helping me keep in contact with all of the aspects of life. I'd especially like to thank Ken for helping me work through not only life but also academic topics by being a font of curiosity and conversation. 

Finally, I would like to thank my parents for their support throughout this journey. I am so grateful to have parents who outwardly voice their support and pride to the end. 
I greatly appreciate everything you've done to ensure I always have a stable world I know I can return to, particularly during the times I was not sure where or how I fit. 
I am especially grateful to my mother for her guidance, and for sharing her own experience as an academic. 

Graduate school was often more challenging and uncertain than I expected, and I am grateful to all of the people whose support helped me persist. 

